{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791534475,"nonce":"5LJ2PPnh1VT+rhM3+MwUGqabN40=","title":"Measured generated WGSL expansion while investigating Ashui renderer memory on macOS. hlwgpu 5706948 pins xgpu-backend 71c25d1. The shader macro correctly emits public static final WGSL; this is not per-frame source allocation.","message":"Ashui shaders generated by hlwgpu HXSL:\n- BackdropShader: 255,549 UTF-8 bytes, 353 functions, including 351 hxsl_value helpers.\n- ShadowShader: 150,581 bytes, 215 functions, including 213 hxsl_value helpers.\n- BoxShader: 74,674 bytes, 123 functions, including 121 hxsl_value helpers.\n- All ten UI shaders: 549,473 source bytes total.\n\nWgslOut.value emits a fresh no-argument helper for each value block following HXSL inlining. These helpers access mutable private state, so textual deduplication or merging without semantic analysis is unsafe. Investigate preserving safe functions or reducing generated value-block expansion before WGSL emission.\n\nIsolation experiment: compiling these same ten shaders and pipelines from Node, using xgpu and the same wgpu backend, increased physical footprint from about 21 MiB after device creation to 53-60 MiB; releasing module handles measured 51-53 MiB. Source text alone is about 0.52 MiB UTF-8 / 1.05 MiB UTF-16. Compiler/driver allocations dominate the source storage. Measurements are physical footprint, not allocation profiling; this does not attribute all retained bytes to Naga or Metal.\n\nAshui is separately changing to cached first-use pipelines and releasing explicit shader/view handles. Track generated-code size and compilation cost here; validate shader semantics, clipping, squircle corners, glass/refraction and GPU pixel parity before any compiler rewrite. Diagnostic data currently in ashui/.ashui/memory-comparison, related Ashui git-bug d701ddf.","files":null}]}